    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d509-a3">

                <pb facs="0712" n="638" xml:id="pg638"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Admiral Mendez to Mr.
                        Hovey.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Headquarters of Her Catholic
                                Majesty’s Squadron in the Pacific,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Frigate Numancia, Harbor of
                            Calloa,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-04-27"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 27, 1866</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor of accompanying the
                    enclosed manifest, in which are expressed the powerful motives which,
                    unfortunately, make necessary the adoption on my part of rigorous measures in
                    return for the unjust aggression of the government of Peru.</p>
                <p>I have no doubt that your excellency, the worthy representative of a friendly
                    government, will be convinced, in view of the facts, of the evident justice that
                    assists Spain.</p>
                <p>I avail myself of his opportunity to offer your excellency my most distinguished
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CASTO MENDEZ NUNEZ.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency the <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister Plenipotentiary</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">of the United States of America resident in
                            Lima</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
